WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.000
Ask five engineers what a service is,

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.910
and you'll get five answers.

3
00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:11.320
Here's the one that makes everything else fall into place:

4
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:13.850
a service is a contract, not a codebase.

5
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.340
Consumers should depend on what a service promises

6
00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.700
— never on how it keeps that promise.

7
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.130
That's the Dependency Inversion Principle.

8
00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:25.600
Chenile makes it something you can see in the file system.

9
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.720
Every Chenile service is two modules.

10
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.050
The api module is pure contract

11
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.210
— the interface and the model.

12
00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:36.770
No implementation, no transport, no framework.

13
00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.560
The service module implements that interface.

14
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.300
And nobody depends on it.

15
00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.210
Open the interface:

16
00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:45.120
one operation, one model.

17
00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:46.790
Now the implementation.

18
00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:47.950
It's almost empty

19
00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:49.650
— just the business line.

20
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:50.200
No auth.

21
00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:50.940
No logging.

22
00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.100
No tenant lookup.

23
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.580
That's deliberate.

24
00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:57.410
Every Chenile service also ships a deep health check,

25
00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:01.930
so an orchestrator knows when to route traffic, or recycle an instance.

26
00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:04.750
Chenile customizes the controller,

27
00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.360
so a service is declared to the framework

28
00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:08.820
— not just exposed.

29
00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:12.390
That declaration creates a seam around every operation.

30
00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:16.420
And that seam is where all the horizontal stuff will attach.

31
00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:18.640
Depend on s1-api.

32
00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:20.730
Never on s1-service.

33
00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:22.190
Next episode:

34
00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:24.820
we generate this from scratch, and run it.

35
00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:27.940
Then we start filling that seam with policies.
